%S A037750 2,23,230,2301,23012,230123,2301230,23012301,230123012,2301230123,
%T A037750 23012301230,230123012301,2301230123012,23012301230123,
%U A037750 230123012301230,2301230123012301,23012301230123012,230123012301230123,2301230123012301230,23012301230123012301
%N A037750 Decimal expansion of a(n) is given by the first n terms of the periodic sequence with initial period 2,3,0,1.
%H A037750 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A037750/b037750.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1000</a>
%H A037750 <a href="/index/Rec#order_05">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (10,0,0,1,-10).
%F A037750 G.f.: ( 2+3*x+x^3 )*x / ( (x-1)*(10*x-1)*(1+x)*(1+x^2) ). - _R. J. Mathar_, Nov 21 2011
%F A037750 From _Elmo R. Oliveira_, Sep 23 2026: (Start)
%F A037750 a(n) = floor(767*10^n/3333).
%F A037750 a(n) = 10*a(n-1) + a(n-4) - 10*a(n-5). (End)
%t A037750 Quotient[767*10^Range[25], 3333] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Sep 23 2026 *)
%t A037750 (* Alternative: *)
%t A037750 LinearRecurrence[{10, 0, 0, 1, -10}, {2, 23, 230, 2301, 23012}, 25] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Sep 23 2026 *)
%o A037750 (PARI) Vec((2+3*x+x^3 )*x/((x-1)*(10*x-1)*(1+x)*(1+x^2)) + O(x^25)) \\ _Jinyuan Wang_, Apr 14 2020
